| `tests.isolation.exempt.<axis>.<test>` | string | `{}` for each axis | `network`, `writes` or `stores`, mapping a test's pytest node id to a non-blank reason | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`load_policy`, `unused_exemptions`), read by `tests/conftest.py` | Lets the named test reach outside its tier on that axis. A blank reason or an unknown axis stops pytest before any test runs (exit 4), and an exemption whose test ran and reached nothing on its axis fails the run; one whose test did not run is not judged. Absent, the guard writes `[using default] tests.isolation.exempt = {}` to stderr. | loosening a whole tier: `tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.<axis>` | always |
